<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">As described in Section <a href="#S3" title="III Knowledge Distillation Optimization for Semantic NOMA (KD-SemNOMA) ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>, CrossKD transfers the intermediate features of the <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer from the student model decoder to the corresponding position of the teacher model decoder for forward propagation, enhancing feature alignment in knowledge distillation (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ III Knowledge Distillation Optimization for Semantic NOMA (KD-SemNOMA) ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). To verify the effect of the choice of <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> on the distillation performance, we conduct the following experiments. Cases include <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A32C3</span> (AWGN, CIFAR-10, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>), <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">R32C3</span> (Rayleigh, CIFAR-10, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>), <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A256C48</span> (AWGN, FFHQ-256, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/48</annotation></semantics></math>), and <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">R256C48</span> (Rayleigh, FFHQ-256, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/48</annotation></semantics></math>). As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ V-B Performance of Knowledge Distillation-Based SemNOMA for Image Transmission ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a>, the first row represents the student model trained without teacher model distillation, using only MAE loss. For <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A32C3</span>, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=4</annotation></semantics></math> (upsampling layer) yields the optimal PSNR/SSIM (33.18/0.973), as upsampling features align well with AWGN’s stable conditions. For <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">R32C3</span>, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=2</annotation></semantics></math> (AF-Module layer) is the best (29.58/0.927), leveraging AF-Module’s adaptation to Rayleigh fading’s variability. In FFHQ-256 cases, <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=5</annotation></semantics></math> performs best (29.24/0.856) for <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A256C48</span> while <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=4</annotation></semantics></math> performs best (27.52/0.818) for <span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">R256C48</span>. These results highlight CrossKD’s ability to optimize layer-specific feature transfer, enhancing decoding performance across diverse datasets and channel conditions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">V-C</span> </span><span id="S5.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Performance of Diffusion-Based Image Refinement for SemNOMA</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, to further improve the perceptual quality of reconstructed images, we evaluate the proposed <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> framework. The first stage leverages knowledge distillation (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ III Knowledge Distillation Optimization for Semantic NOMA (KD-SemNOMA) ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) to optimize the proposed <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA</span> network, improving PSNR and SSIM for initial reconstructions <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\text{init}}=\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\text{init}}=\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S2.E4" title="In II-A Overview ‣ II System Model ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). The second stage utilizes the diffusion model and employs DDIM sampling (<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}=100</annotation></semantics></math>, Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ IV-B Diffusion-Based Image Refinement ‣ IV Diffusion Model-Based Image Refinement ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) to refine <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\text{init}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\text{init}}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S4.E23" title="In IV-B Diffusion-Based Image Refinement ‣ IV Diffusion Model-Based Image Refinement ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), enhancing LPIPS and FID perceptual quality under challenging channel conditions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Simulations are conducted under AWGN and Rayleigh fading channels with the compression ratio <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/48</annotation></semantics></math>, across SNR <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> ranges from -5 to 20 dB. We compare the proposed <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> scheme against CGAN based image refinement <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA-CGAN</span>, and the one-stage schemes (<span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KD-SemNOMA</span>, <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA</span>, <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DeepJSCC-NOMA</span>). As shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F9" title="Fig. 9 ‣ V-B Performance of Knowledge Distillation-Based SemNOMA for Image Transmission ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> achieves superior LPIPS and FID across all SNR levels, with particularly notable improvements in the low SNR range of [-5, 5] dB. For instance, at <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> = 0dB under AWGN channel, <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> significantly reduces the LPIPS and FID values compared with the one-stage method, indicating that the utilize of the diffusion model greatly improves the perceptual quality of the received image. At the same time, compared with <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA-CGAN</span>, <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> reduces the LPIPS and FID values by approximately <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="23\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>23</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">23\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="36\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>36</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">36\%</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, reflecting the image generation advantages of the diffusion model over the CGAN model and its robustness to severe channel noise.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed scheme <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> outperforms <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA-CGAN</span>, as diffusion models capture richer image distributions and recover finer details, leading to lower LPIPS and FID scores. Unlike GAN-based methods, which often struggle with mode collapse and artifacts in low-SNR scenarios, the iterative denoising of the diffusion model (Eq. <a href="#S4.E25" title="In IV-B Diffusion-Based Image Refinement ‣ IV Diffusion Model-Based Image Refinement ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) effectively mitigates channel-induced distortions, especially at <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[-5,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[-5,5]</annotation></semantics></math> dB. Additionally, the accelerated sampling with <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}=100</annotation></semantics></math> (compared to DDPM’s <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\approx 1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\approx 1000</annotation></semantics></math>) ensures computational efficiency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. These results underscore the efficacy of combining knowledge distillation and diffusion-based refinement for high-fidelity multi-user image reconstruction.</p>
</div>
