</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 11</span>: </span><span id="S5.F11.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Examples of reconstructed images under Rayleigh channel with <math id="S5.F11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math> dB.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We provide examples of reconstructed images from FFHQ-256 datasets in Fig. <a href="#S5.F10" title="Fig. 10 ‣ V-C Performance of Diffusion-Based Image Refinement for SemNOMA ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S5.F11" title="Fig. 11 ‣ V-C Performance of Diffusion-Based Image Refinement for SemNOMA ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, showcasing visual quality at <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math> dB under AWGN and Rayleigh fading channels, respectively. While <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KD-SemNOMA</span> and <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA-CGAN</span> achieve competitive PSNR and SSIM for initial reconstructions <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\text{init}}=\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\text{init}}=\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, their images suffer from noise-induced degradation at <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math> dB, losing semantic details such as facial contours. <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA-CGAN</span>, relying on GAN-based generation, often introduces artifacts and blurred textures, particularly under Rayleigh fading, due to mode collapse in low-SNR conditions. In contrast, <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> leverages error contraction in the forward diffusion process (Eq. <a href="#S4.E24" title="In IV-B Diffusion-Based Image Refinement ‣ IV Diffusion Model-Based Image Refinement ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) and iterative denoising with diffusion priors (Eq. <a href="#S4.E25" title="In IV-B Diffusion-Based Image Refinement ‣ IV Diffusion Model-Based Image Refinement ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), achieving superior LPIPS and FID scores. Visualizations demonstrate that <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KDD-SemNOMA</span> restores finer facial details, such as hair textures and eye clarity, outperforming <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SemNOMA-CGAN</span> by producing more natural and perceptually coherent images <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">V-D</span> </span><span id="S5.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Ablation Study</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the effectiveness of the knowledge distillation optimization scheme in enhancing model performance, we conduct ablation studies using following datasets (CIFAR-10, FFHQ-256), compression ratios (1/3, 1/48), and channel conditions (AWGN, Rayleigh) at <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=10</annotation></semantics></math> dB. Results are presented in Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="TABLE IV ‣ V-D Ablation Study ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a>, with cases defined as follows: <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A32C3</span> (AWGN, CIFAR-10, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>), <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">R32C3</span> (Rayleigh, CIFAR-10, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>), <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A256C48</span> (AWGN, FFHQ-256, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/48</annotation></semantics></math>), and <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">R256C48</span> (Rayleigh, FFHQ-256, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/48</annotation></semantics></math>). The first row represents the baseline where only reconstruction loss is used, indicating that the student model is trained without distillation from the teacher model. The subsequent rows demonstrate the performance of the student model trained with different distillation algorithms. Specifically, the second and third rows confirm that both FA and CrossKD distillation improve model performance. The final row indicates that the best performance is achieved when FA and CrossKD are applied simultaneously.
Notably, performance gains are consistent across datasets and channels. These findings align with results in Fig. <a href="#S5.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ V-B Performance of Knowledge Distillation-Based SemNOMA for Image Transmission ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S5.F7" title="Fig. 7 ‣ V-B Performance of Knowledge Distillation-Based SemNOMA for Image Transmission ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> for CIFAR-10 and Fig. <a href="#S5.F8" title="Fig. 8 ‣ V-B Performance of Knowledge Distillation-Based SemNOMA for Image Transmission ‣ V Training and Evaluation ‣ Knowledge Distillation Driven Semantic NOMA for Image Transmission with Diffusion Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> for FFHQ-256.</p>
</div>
